  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Liturgical chant of the Georgian Orthodox Church, sung in an indigenous three-part polyphony and handed down orally through regional schools such as those of Gelati in Imereti, Shemokmedi in Guria and the Kartli-Kakhetian tradition associated with the Karbelashvili family. Chanters including the Karbelashvili brothers transcribed large parts of the repertoire into staff notation, and after Soviet-era suppression church choirs revived the chant from these transcriptions.",
